 compiles and behaves: parameters introduced with `of`, a buffer
 parameter and a text parameter, a buffer declared INSIDE the body from a
 format string that interpolates the text parameter, and `'s size` and
 `byte 1 of` read off the buffer parameter. The manual elides the body
 with `...`; the three statements it does show are reproduced verbatim
 and their values printed. `byte 1 of hay` is 65, the ASCII code of the
 `A` the caller passed, which pins the 1-indexing at the same time.
